---
import Layout from '@ui/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '@core/config/site';

// One address, read from config, so the site cannot advertise a channel the legal
// pages do not also point at. If site.email ever changes, every route in and out
// changes with it.
const email = site.email;
---

<Layout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach Studely — corrections to an offer, suggestions, privacy requests, or anything else."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h1>Get in touch</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Studely is run by one person, so email is the only channel — but it is read by a
        human rather than a helpdesk.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>What is worth writing about</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>An offer is wrong or dead.</strong> The most useful message I can get.
          Include the offer and what you saw — a broken link, a price that changed,
          eligibility rules that no longer match. Corrections get priority over everything
          else.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An offer is missing.</strong> Send the provider's own page rather than a
          referral link. It will be read, checked and scored by the same criteria as
          everything already listed; being suggested does not get anything listed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>You disagree with a score.</strong> Every point is named on the offer's
          page, so tell me which reason is wrong and why. That is a more useful argument
          than the number itself, and it has changed scores before.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy and your data.</strong> Access, correction, deletion, or anything
          else under GDPR — see the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for what is
          held. Almost nothing is: no account is needed to read the directory.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Something looks like a security problem.</strong> Please write before
          publishing it anywhere.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <p>
        There is no support team and no promised response time — one person answers when
        they can. What I will not do is leave a reported dead link sitting there: the
        catalogue is the whole product, and a listing that is wrong is worse than a listing
        that is missing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Studely is not the provider of any offer. If your problem is with a signup,
        eligibility check, billing or refund, that has to go to the provider directly —
        their terms govern it, not ours. See <a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
